00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:51.060
Those earnings are gonna be key.

00:06:51.060 --> 00:06:52.020
Watch out for that.

00:06:52.020 --> 00:06:54.120
Last thing we wanna talk
about here on "Market Takes"

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:55.620
is the weak dollar.

00:06:55.620 --> 00:06:57.270
There's been all kinds of talk about this,

00:06:57.270 --> 00:06:58.410
folks have been worried.

00:06:58.410 --> 00:07:00.840
News headlines popping up here and there.

00:07:00.840 --> 00:07:03.910
Also, you've seen Secretary
of the Treasury, Janet Yellen,

00:07:03.910 --> 00:07:06.240
gave an interview where
she was asked directly

00:07:06.240 --> 00:07:07.260
about the state of the dollar.

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:09.060
So, wanna throw something
on your screen here,

00:07:09.060 --> 00:07:11.760
really quickly, to just show
you the movement overall.

00:07:11.760 --> 00:07:13.980
You see there, the dollar
is clearly down this year

00:07:13.980 --> 00:07:15.480
but that movement has been up and down,

00:07:15.480 --> 00:07:17.700
and you see at the edge of
your screen there on the right,

00:07:17.700 --> 00:07:18.750
picking back up.

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:21.780
Investors are very strongly
positioned right now,

00:07:21.780 --> 00:07:24.630
speculative investors, for a big pickup

00:07:24.630 --> 00:07:27.300
and an increase in the dollar this year,

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:29.130
their position net long on the dollar

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:31.350
against just about every other
major currency out there.

00:07:31.350 --> 00:07:32.790
So, that chart illustrating

00:07:32.790 --> 00:07:35.220
the overall positioning
right now, that we've seen,

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:37.020
we've seen the dollar
decline a little bit.

00:07:37.020 --> 00:07:39.960
It's weaker, but historically
not that big a move.

00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:42.510
I wanna read you a real quick
quote from Secretary Yellen.

00:07:42.510 --> 00:07:44.400
She said, quote, "There is a risk

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:45.810
when we use financial sanctions

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:47.460
that are linked to the role of the dollar,

00:07:47.460 --> 00:07:49.500
that over time it could undermine

00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:51.270
the hegemony of the dollar."

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:53.100
What that means is the
value of the dollar,

00:07:53.100 --> 00:07:56.040
the ability and the
omnipresence of the dollar

00:07:56.040 --> 00:07:58.890
in global financial systems,
there's a risk there.

00:07:58.890 --> 00:08:00.930
We've seen talk from China, from Russia,

00:08:00.930 --> 00:08:03.480
there's been a long-term
push against the dollar

00:08:03.480 --> 00:08:04.830
because they don't want the United States

00:08:04.830 --> 00:08:07.700
to be able to sanction them
to cause economic pain.

00:08:07.700 --> 00:08:09.060
If they don't use the dollar,

00:08:09.060 --> 00:08:11.310
well, the US can't cut them
outta the banking system,

00:08:11.310 --> 00:08:12.143
et cetera, et cetera.

00:08:12.143 --> 00:08:13.782
But, as you saw from that chart,

00:08:13.782 --> 00:08:16.560
the dollar has declined
in value a little bit,

00:08:16.560 --> 00:08:18.480
but investors not buying that story,

00:08:18.480 --> 00:08:20.292
thinking, "Okay, the
dollar's power and strength

00:08:20.292 --> 00:08:21.540
is gonna come back,"

00:08:21.540 --> 00:08:23.910
and that over the course
of time, over the course,

00:08:23.910 --> 00:08:25.530
even of this year, we'll be back.

00:08:25.530 --> 00:08:27.990
We are at historically-strong
levels for the dollar

00:08:27.990 --> 00:08:29.569
and folks are thinking,
"Okay, that dollar strength

00:08:29.569 --> 00:08:32.310
is gonna come back because
maybe interest rates

00:08:32.310 --> 00:08:33.143
are picking up."

00:08:33.143 --> 00:08:35.370
This really is a story more
about the Federal Reserve

00:08:35.370 --> 00:08:36.480
and central banks,

00:08:36.480 --> 00:08:38.700
and the expectation for
the European Central Bank

00:08:38.700 --> 00:08:40.260
to raise rates more than the Fed.

00:08:40.260 --> 00:08:42.230
This isn't about people
not using the dollar

00:08:42.230 --> 00:08:43.680
or the dollar going away.

00:08:43.680 --> 00:08:44.820
Just wanted to make that clear.

00:08:44.820 --> 00:08:46.770
And this week we will hear from the Fed.

